            "review_title": "Review at Tropical Fruit",
            "review_text": "rod4mac\nMontreal, Canada6 contributions\n1\nFruit to go, juices smoothies, burgers and pizza\nApr 2016 • Solo\nTropical Fruit at 62 Hùng Vương has the best smoothies and juices at the lowest prices that I have found in Nha Trang. They also have a modest meal menu including an excellent hamburger. I found it better than another one rated “best\" in Nha Trang (if you get the double patty). I had a generous double cheeseburger with fries and a can of beer for 82,000 dong, about US$3.70. They also have chicken burgers (not my thing) and decent small pizzas. I prefer Vietnamese food while in Vietnam, but get a craving for a burger once in a while.\n\nThere are two other reasons to drop by Tropical Fruit. \n\nFirst, the three sisters who run the show are friendly and cheerful and speak enough English for you to ask them to diminish or omit sugar in your fruit drink. (Important in Nha Trang.) They can also explain things about the fruit they also sell -don’t be afraid to ask how to peel and eat dragon fruit and papaya, or the name of those hairy things (delicious Rambutan).\n\nSecond is Su-su. Su-su is a thirty-six year old dog. She does not immediately mix with customers, but you can woo her with patience. :-)\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten April 5, 2016",
